Z||000020||pontiacs4me||08-09-2001||02:20 AM||||At 18 I built a 1973 firebird formula from scratch.  I must of had parts on that car from every firebird from every salvage in town.  At 21 I bought my first fiero, and did a 2.5 to 2.8 swap by myself in 30 hours labor.  Thats including pulling it out of the donor car, off the manual and onto the auto.  <BR>Just buy a manual, label your wires, take your time, and when you get pissed, walk away for awhile.  Anger will make the job bigger.||||reg||1
